# RoboticelaOS runtime plan

Phase + goal number + short name. Each phase ends with a **wire/integrate** goal against all completed phases.

Completed stack today: **Phases 0–13**, **15–18** (HTML/CSS complete; RoboJS host-complete; Compositor wired).
**Active premium path (ASAP shell first):** **Phase 14** → remaining **Phase 19** paint/layout depth the shell needs → **44 → 45 → 46 → 47**.
Do not reorder past the ASAP shell track in Phase 14 to chase later product surfaces.

---

## Application & UI doctrine (standing rule for every app)

Every product surface — Desktop shell, Settings, Finder-class apps, future third-party apps — follows the same performance model. This is not optional architecture.

```text
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│  Roboticela React package (@roboticela/react)                 │
│  Author UI in React on the host. Bindings map JS calls → C. │
│  Guest never runs a React reconciler / VDOM.                 │
└───────────────┬─────────────────────────────┬───────────────┘
                │ SSR / export                │ command / bridge
                ▼                             ▼
     HTML + CSS (design)              RoboJS (thin) → DesktopBridge
     RoboHTML / RoboCSS /             allowlisted verbs only
     Layout / Paint                   │
                │                     ▼
                └──────────►     C runtime (behavior)
                                 RoboDesktop / Input / Compositor /
                                 Window / future RoboOS Native API
```

| Layer | Owns | Must not own |
|---|---|---|
| **C** | Window manager, focus, drag/resize, z-order, input capture, clipboard, compositor present, system commands, app launch, performance-critical logic | Per-frame layout authored as ad-hoc pixel math inside React |
| **HTML + CSS** | Look of window **content** and document chrome that paints through the document pipeline | Pointer-driven WM (move/resize every mousemove) |
| **Roboticela React package** | Host authoring components, design tokens, `data-command` / bridge helpers, SSR export to `DesktopPage.h` | A second JS engine; guest React; unrestricted FFI |
| **RoboJS** | Click/handlers that call bridge verbs; tiny DOM updates for status | Window manager; full SPA; Chromium/V8 |

**Performance rule:** pointer motion, frame present, and window chrome stay in **C**. JS is a **command bus** (`data-command` / bridge API) that executes **C**. Apps that follow this get the best frame pacing this runtime can deliver; apps that drive the desk from RoboJS every frame will jank.

**React rule:** React is the **design/devkit** language. Build with Vite on the host; export static HTML/CSS + a small page script for the guest. `14.x` React runtime rule forbids shipping a guest React runtime.

**Chromium lesson (reference only):** Aura/Views-class chrome and compositor stay native; content is a document. Never add Blink/V8/Skia.

